  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "af07a7eb-adab-4ae6-864f-0a01e146bb75",
    "name": "PatientReferralManagementAPI",
    "description": "This collection contains the core REST requests for the **Patient Referral Management API**. It’s organized around two main resources—**patients** and **referrals**—and provides a complete set of endpoints to create, retrieve, update, delete, and list these resources.\n\n**What you can do with this collection**\n\n- **Patients**\n    \n    - Create a patient (`POST /api/patients`)\n        \n    - List patients (`GET /api/patients`)\n        \n    - Get, update, and delete a specific patient (`GET/PUT/DELETE /api/patients/:id`)\n        \n    - Retrieve referrals for a patient (`GET /api/patients/:id/referrals`)\n        \n- **Referrals**\n    \n    - Create a referral (`POST /api/referrals`)\n        \n    - List referrals with pagination (`GET /api/referrals?page=1&size=10`)\n        \n    - Get, update, and delete a specific referral (`GET/PUT/DELETE /api/referrals/:id`)\n        \n\n**How it’s structured**\n\n- Requests are grouped under an `api` folder, then split into `patients` and `referrals`, with nested `{id}` subfolders for operations on specific resources.\n    \n\n**Configuration**\n\n- All requests use the `{{baseUrl}}` environment variable so the same collection can be run against different environments (e.g., dev/prod) by switching environments.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "53735"
  },
